WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.967
Edit 0.016 percent

00:00:02.779 --> 00:00:03.475
of weights

00:00:03.605 --> 00:00:04.666
fix the reasoning

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:06.864
Qwen 3.5 0

00:00:06.676 --> 00:00:07.218
.

00:00:07.112 --> 00:00:08.456
8B often repeated

00:00:08.268 --> 00:00:09.399
its reasoning until

00:00:09.211 --> 00:00:09.824
it hit the

00:00:09.636 --> 00:00:10.520
token limit

00:00:10.662 --> 00:00:11.888
before ever reaching

00:00:11.699 --> 00:00:12.454
an answer

00:00:12.982 --> 00:00:14.019
The fix with

00:00:13.831 --> 00:00:15.175
no gradient descent

00:00:15.329 --> 00:00:16.802
subtract one direction

00:00:16.614 --> 00:00:18.123
from 64 neurons'

00:00:17.935 --> 00:00:19.055
output weights in

00:00:18.866 --> 00:00:20.305
layers 15 and

00:00:20.116 --> 00:00:20.918
19

00:00:21.057 --> 00:00:24.111
That's 131,072 of

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.608
about 800 million

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:26.080
weights

00:00:26.606 --> 00:00:28.598
TabbyML's WebGPU demo

00:00:28.457 --> 00:00:29.223
lets you watch

00:00:29.035 --> 00:00:29.459
it

00:00:29.598 --> 00:00:31.060
The original experiment

00:00:30.872 --> 00:00:33.112
raised MATH-500 accuracy

00:00:32.924 --> 00:00:34.551
from 7.9 to

00:00:34.363 --> 00:00:36.143
48.1 percent

00:00:36.678 --> 00:00:37.692
Full story on

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:38.399
the dashboard
